WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.407
- I'm with a large group
of slow-moving people,

00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:06.515
and this is really helping me.

00:00:06.515 --> 00:00:08.954
(acoustic guitar strumming)

00:00:08.954 --> 00:00:11.948
- Fidget Spinners are
not just a cool new toy.

00:00:11.948 --> 00:00:14.486
They are supposed to be a tool

00:00:14.486 --> 00:00:18.720
to help people with
ADHD and anxiety focus.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.562
- I've had ADHD as long as I can remember.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:23.492
- People who have ADD,
when you're not focused

00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:25.312
your brain is going everywhere.

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:28.598
- When I saw the Fidget Spinner,
it never jumped out to me

00:00:28.598 --> 00:00:30.927
as something that would help my ADHD.

00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:35.094
- ADHD can cause some fidgeting
and body control issues.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.796
Your brain is chronically under-aroused,

00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:40.178
meaning it's kind of bored.

00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:41.429
- I'll play with my hair.

00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:45.099
And I have split ends, and so
it's like a little project.

00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:47.467
- I'm really bad at sitting or standing

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:50.375
to watch or listen to something
for a long period of time.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:52.018
- Yeah, I fidget constantly.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.950
- I probably interrupt more than I fidget.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.407
- And I lean back in my chair like this.

00:00:56.407 --> 00:00:58.381
- Repetitive motions
like cracking knuckles,

00:00:58.381 --> 00:01:02.554
or sitting funny in their
chair, or tapping their feet.

00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:04.604
As long as that's something
that functions for them,

00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:06.545
then it's a fidget that
doesn't interfere with focus.

00:01:06.545 --> 00:01:07.834
It probably actually helps it.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.012
The claims that Fidget
Spinners are backed by science

00:01:11.012 --> 00:01:14.840
as useful tools for people with
ADHD are somewhat overblown.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.441
They keep it vague because
there actually isn't

00:01:16.441 --> 00:01:18.584
a whole lot to support these specifically.

00:01:18.584 --> 00:01:20.671
- It seems like it doesn't
serve many purposes.

00:01:20.671 --> 00:01:22.132
I feel like I would get, after a while,

00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:23.597
I would get bored of this.

00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:25.158
- I guess I don't really know until I try.

00:01:25.158 --> 00:01:26.616
- Fidget Spinners are more likely

00:01:26.616 --> 00:01:28.997
to be a distraction and a toy,

00:01:28.997 --> 00:01:31.912
but there are adults who
can make that determination

00:01:31.912 --> 00:01:33.305
a little bit better for themselves.

00:01:33.305 --> 00:01:35.320
And so, if they are able
to get more work done,

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.381
or they are able to sit through meetings,

00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:39.558
or get through the tasks in their day,

00:01:39.558 --> 00:01:42.218
then I would say that it probably works.

00:01:42.218 --> 00:01:43.748
- I have a lot of work to do today.

00:01:43.748 --> 00:01:45.660
I came into work early this morning.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.493
Hopefully, this works.

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:52.149
- [Andrew] Using it at
PyCon in Portland this year.

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:53.477
If anyone asks, I'll just tell them

00:01:53.477 --> 00:01:54.788
we're doing an experiment.

00:01:54.788 --> 00:01:57.495
- And hopefully, I don't
get distracted doing stuff

00:01:57.495 --> 00:01:59.288
like fidgeting around on my desk.

00:01:59.288 --> 00:02:02.640
Well, I put my hair up so
that I wouldn't play with it.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.971
- Has the fidget spinning annoyed you?

00:02:04.971 --> 00:02:07.667
- It's probably distracted
me more than it's helped her.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.773
- Just came out of the meaning
with my Fidget Spinner.

00:02:09.773 --> 00:02:12.154
And this is a meeting
where shouting out a lot,

00:02:12.154 --> 00:02:14.366
because I won't pay
attention if I don't do that,

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.266
and I didn't say anything.

00:02:16.266 --> 00:02:17.183
It's a win.

00:02:18.141 --> 00:02:19.686
- I'm going to try to use a Fidget Spinner

00:02:19.686 --> 00:02:21.078
while I watch a TV show,

00:02:21.078 --> 00:02:24.262
'cause that is when I
tend to move around a lot.

00:02:24.262 --> 00:02:26.412
- [Andrew] When I talk to
people, I'll pull it out

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.879
and start fidgeting with it.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:31.230
I think it's not well received by them.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.719
- It's getting kind of
tedious to use this.

00:02:34.719 --> 00:02:37.122
It makes this lie whoosh sound,

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:39.497
and it kinda distracts my brain.

00:02:39.497 --> 00:02:43.952
Instead of using the Fidget
Spinner, I'm just eating grapes.

00:02:43.952 --> 00:02:45.920
So it's not really doing much.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.830
- [Andrew] It does help me
focus when I'm talking to people

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.784
because I know what I'm
doing with my hands.

00:02:49.784 --> 00:02:51.217
Often, I'll find myself in
a crowd, and I'll be like,

00:02:51.217 --> 00:02:52.498
"What do I do with my hands?"

00:02:52.498 --> 00:02:55.163
- We're about to get on
a train for eight hours.

00:02:55.163 --> 00:02:58.782
The thing keeps spinning, so
it's always doing something.

00:02:58.782 --> 00:03:01.528
I really didn't think the
Fidget Spinner was gonna work.

00:03:01.528 --> 00:03:02.816
It works.

00:03:02.816 --> 00:03:04.400
I would use the Fidget Spinner so much,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.561
and then I would put my hand down,

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:08.546
and my hand would get tingly,
and it would need the spinner.

00:03:08.546 --> 00:03:09.399
It was crazy.

00:03:09.399 --> 00:03:11.483
- So as the week goes on, we're all having

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:15.288
a lot of trouble not losing this thing.

00:03:15.288 --> 00:03:16.992
It's very lose-able.

00:03:16.992 --> 00:03:18.461
- It never got permanently lost,

00:03:18.461 --> 00:03:21.502
but I would misplace it
probably every other day.

00:03:21.502 --> 00:03:23.975
- I had it this morning and ...

00:03:23.975 --> 00:03:24.808
Found it.

00:03:26.281 --> 00:03:28.615
So we're just coming
back from a long weekend

00:03:28.615 --> 00:03:30.328
of looking at wedding venues.

00:03:30.328 --> 00:03:33.920
And the Fidget Spinner
actually was helpful

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.356
with my anxiety, which was high.

00:03:37.356 --> 00:03:38.784
- It didn't do much for me.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:41.612
As someone with ADHD,
it was just another item

00:03:41.612 --> 00:03:43.323
for me to lose all the time.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.531
- I thought it was gonna be stupid

00:03:44.531 --> 00:03:47.056
but it really, I really liked it.

00:03:47.056 --> 00:03:48.619
It really works.

00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:51.521
- The amount this distracts other people

00:03:51.521 --> 00:03:53.890
doesn't warrant the
amount it helps me focus.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.330
- I got a bruise here 'cause I would just

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.632
do it so hard, 'cause it was like,

00:03:57.632 --> 00:04:00.019
I just loved the fact
that you just like ...

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:02.290
- I thought it was helping
me focus in meetings,

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:06.434
but maybe it was just
giving me something else

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.769
to focus on so I wasn't
so annoying in meetings.

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:11.063
- I think a really good
test for whether or not

00:04:11.063 --> 00:04:13.443
a Fidget Spinner is
something useful would be,

00:04:13.443 --> 00:04:15.057
"What did you remember from the meeting?"

00:04:15.057 --> 00:04:16.355
It might be a distraction,

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:19.765
but it might not be an attention focuser.

00:04:19.765 --> 00:04:22.075
- And so I'd bring it with
me, but I'd often misplace it.

00:04:22.075 --> 00:04:23.852
And I think that actually speaks,

00:04:23.852 --> 00:04:26.248
the way that an ADHD brain works.

00:04:26.248 --> 00:04:28.465
For some people it can kinda
be another distraction.

00:04:28.465 --> 00:04:29.681
- I was chatting with a whole bunch

00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:31.348
of other engineers at the conference.

00:04:31.348 --> 00:04:34.032
This kinda gave me a little
something to focus on

00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:36.575
besides the crowd as I was
engaging with other people.

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:40.731
It prevented that brief moment of boredom

00:04:40.731 --> 00:04:43.639
that usually leads to getting
distracted with the ADHD.

00:04:43.639 --> 00:04:45.694
- My huge issue is I was always
playing with my split ends.

00:04:45.694 --> 00:04:47.035
That was a really big issue for me.

00:04:47.035 --> 00:04:49.305
Any time I felt myself doing
it, I would just pick up

00:04:49.305 --> 00:04:52.090
my Fidget Spinner, and
I would just do this.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.117
- I don't recommend this for ADHD.

00:04:54.117 --> 00:04:56.010
I recommend it for anxiety.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.628
Looking at venues, and I
had my Fidget Spinner out.

00:04:58.628 --> 00:05:02.413
Every time I heard a
per-person price for food,

00:05:02.413 --> 00:05:05.790
I could have had a panic
attack, but I didn't.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.130
You have to be in a
situation where it's not

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.215
annoying people when you're using it.

00:05:09.215 --> 00:05:10.846
And it's not gonna work for everyone.

00:05:10.846 --> 00:05:12.653
But if you want to try it, try it.

00:05:12.653 --> 00:05:15.486
(acoustic guitar)

